          %h2#Idea Idea
          %p
            For
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %msub
                    %mi U
                    %mi i
                  %mo →
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{U_i \to X\}
            a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cover"} cover
            of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/space"} space
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            %strong Čech groupoid
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internal+groupoid"} internal groupoid
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %msub
                    %mi U
                    %mi i
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo =
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                  %mstyle{:displaystyle => "false"}
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∐
                        %mrow
                          %mi i
                          %mi j
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi i
                    %mo ∩
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi j
                    %mo ⇉
                    %mstyle{:displaystyle => "false"}
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∐
                          %mi i
                      %msub
                        %mi U
                        %mi i
                      %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mo ,
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  C\big(\{U_i\}\big)
                  \\;=\;
                  \\big(
                  \\textstyle{\coprod_{i j}} U_i \cap U_j
                  \\rightrightarrows
                  \\textstyle{\coprod_i} U_i
                  \\big)
                  \\,,
          %p
            whose object of objects is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/disjoint+union"} disjoint union
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∐
                    %mi i
                  %msub
                    %mi U
                    %mi i
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \coprod_i U_i
            of the covering patches, and whose object of morphisms is the disjoint union of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/intersections"} intersections
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi U
                    %mi i
                  %mo ∩
                  %msub
                    %mi U
                    %mi j
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U_i \cap U_j
            of these patches.
          %p
            The Čech groupoid is the
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 2
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coskeleton"} coskeleton
            of the full
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%C4%8Cech+nerve"} Čech nerve
          %p
            The following graphics illustrates the Čhech groupoid of a (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/good+open+cover"} good
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/open+cover"} open cover
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/open+disk"} open disk
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi 𝔻
                    %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{D}^{2}
            by three
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/charts"} charts
            (indicated in light gray is the space of objects, and in darker gray the space of non-identity morpshisms):
          %div{:style => "margin: -30px 0px 20px 30px"}
            %img{:src => "/nlab/files/CechGroupoid-Illustration-251101b.png", :width => "700px"}/
          %p
            If we speak about
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generalized+element"} generalized points
            of the
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi U
                    %mi i
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U_i
            (which are often just ordinary points, in applications), then
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                an
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/object"} object
                of
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                      %msub
                        %mi U
                        %mi i
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C(\{U_i\})
                is a pair
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo ,
                      %mi i
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (x,i)
                where
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
                is a point in
                = succeed ";" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi U
                          %mi i
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U_i
            %li
              %p
                there is a unique
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphism"} morphism
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo ,
                      %mi i
                      %mo ,
                      %mi j
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo ,
                      %mi i
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo →
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo ,
                      %mi j
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (x,i,j) \,\colon\, (x,i) \to (x,j)
                for all pairs of objects labeled by the same
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
                such that
                = succeed ";" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi x
                        %mo ∈
                        %msub
                          %mi U
                          %mi i
                        %mo ∩
                        %msub
                          %mi U
                          %mi j
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \in U_i \cap U_j
            %li
              %p
                hence the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/composition"} composition
                of morphisms is of this form:
          %svg{:height => "97.661pt", :version => "1.2", :viewbox => "0 0 249.734 97.661", :width => "249.734pt", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/2000/svg", "xmlns:xlink" => "http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"}
